  "transcript": "Canonical serialization rule: take the proposal artifact EXACTLY as given, serialize it as JSON with sorted keys and no whitespace, and persist the exact bytes hashed as proposal_canon.json in the run scratch dir; then compute hProposal = SHA-256(proposal_canon.json) and seed = SHA-256(hProposal + salt) (with the engine-provided salt), where a third party can re-derive seedHex by repeating the same canonical serialization, hashing proposal_canon.json to reproduce hProposal, concatenating hProposal with the provided salt, and hashing again to obtain seedHex."
